  "structure": {
    "block_count": 49,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "Ready to Conceive at 35 (or Older)? These Tips Can Help You Feel Confident and Prepared",
        "text_sha256": "1cfe11414773eba8399b3c2203d9d23c904cf7ac03fb33d9a41c06c9956a9d3f",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "by Heidi Murkoff , author of What to Expect When You're Expecting.",
        "text_sha256": "fe0f379871761f84993fc97638e1be60dfaee98ef922ce30fb241d275bfed786",
        "word_count": 12
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Updates to copy, sources, and formatting.",
        "text_sha256": "2bf448333081ffc8549a45a6c4b7fc711ee4b93575f0fffd3c4a6212c13581c2",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Unrecognizable woman talking to a doctor",
        "text_sha256": "e0e4eb0fa7f801304260ffbede7299fcb18caf7788f1871d3873513df686348f",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "What to know about your odds of getting pregnant if you're over 35, including tips and managing potential risks.",
        "text_sha256": "c3f6ecf49769204540ae1e1284806c53c216a54dc95e922e3347058e09c2d87d",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I'm 37 years old, and I want to have a baby. What are my chances of getting pregnant? And are there special concerns for women my age that I should be aware of?\"",
        "text_sha256": "4fbe13415afdf40d372c1ebeddf0b84f7b8fb3c66ee919c146980929be5feea5",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "You can absolutely still get pregnant — it may just take a little longer. While fertility does dip with age, plenty of people conceive in their late 30s and beyond.",
        "text_sha256": "76258520de6fcc229e4d864c3193e3c2379a1cf9632ca893b8e8bff1e932ed1d",
        "word_count": 30
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "A few smart pre-TTC moves can boost your odds. Book a preconception visit; learn your cycle so you can time sex around ovulation; and focus on the basics: good food, solid sleep, regular exercise, and a prenatal vitamin.",
        "text_sha256": "c2f5df16204aec3499d9be150f328fba688650da0ff2f2ca4629fd146ba83f7e",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Once you’re pregnant, expect a little extra monitoring — and lots of reassurance. Your provider may keep a closer eye on things like blood pressure and gestational diabetes and offer additional prenatal testing, but with good care and healthy habits, most 35+ pregnancies go smoothly.",
        "text_sha256": "90769011ec9e67a2325197cf79ccd3d1742b2363ebb26f5317a218ef03b0b3df",
        "word_count": 45
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Welcome to the 35-plus club! You won't be the only one in the maternity ward (or, down the road, on the elementary school PTA) in her late 30s or 40s. With birthrates soaring for women 35 and up, there's never been a more popular — or safer — time to be pregnant at any age.",
        "text_sha256": "30d9bd6c4184715dddf314007af58e1b833e5852a81bc16c1875917b8ae1446b",
        "word_count": 55
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "While it may take a bit longer to get pregnant if you're 35 or older, the average time it takes to conceive is still high. Women under 25 have a 25% chance of conceiving per cycle, compared to 15% among women between 35 and 39 years old. The rate drops to 5 to 1% by age 40.",
        "text_sha256": "0d97dc8e2425f1c85c90fea7b9a4bfd6c377c238d1a28b3399e4a1300292ee88",
        "word_count": 57
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Ready to make a baby? Be sure to take a few important steps to boost your odds of conceiving:",
        "text_sha256": "b3100e84eb7d75cda46ee6bbe961c3401963019d593ff59f633c186bf47a7d06",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Make a preconception appointment with your practitioner to make sure all is well.",
        "text_sha256": "8d0b5a2ecf40d170e21caedfb1168b63f5b9ea85157827f12945fec1e9f16f54",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Know your cycle, so you know when to take advantage of baby-making opportunities.",
        "text_sha256": "b0c85444c2fd2cd94509d2abe27b064a44a3c296520fa450fa1ddc6a9bb5d2b9",
        "word_count": 13
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Stay healthy by eating well, getting enough sleep, exercising regularly, and taking a prenatal vitamin .",
        "text_sha256": "a678227583ba833b2885735c1a4270ecaa5ce111481484f08a2e5466745c0b16",
        "word_count": 16
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you try for more than six months without success, seek advice from your doctor. Even if a fertility issue is discovered, there's still an excellent chance that it can be resolved so that you can become pregnant.",
        "text_sha256": "356a9f4520ad7782208bd74633e5a609b6b342b6f48d8224b953e6e06c7bfbbb",
        "word_count": 38
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Once you do conceive, your practitioner will monitor you closely for common, treatable pregnancy-related problems including high blood pressure and gestational diabetes (which occur slightly more frequently in older moms-to-be), and offer up a slew of prenatal tests to check on your baby's health (just to be on the safe side).",
        "text_sha256": "67a42cd0c1f6ed78ebf0aef47d62d08e5027cb030e1f7f7d351ffb8f27f05d5f",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Rest assured, given healthy habits and the right medical care, women over 35 can and do have easy, healthy pregnancies as well as smooth deliveries. With any luck, the worst thing you'll have to worry about is being identified by your practitioner as someone of \"advanced maternal age\" (yuck!).",
        "text_sha256": "81a5763bc6846f8275247aeea3b7cefb91e3237b63efb17bfd8bb9e5d880409d",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Good luck,",
        "text_sha256": "025f1bc4e552180371e36b8972e979b175a33ae7a72003900fd0ce28611e29d9",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Heidi Murkoff",
        "text_sha256": "6f05d1b1394d028842497499fff96bffb14810fb4a10d1a23a1ef1b82a72292e",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "blockquote",
        "tag": "blockquote",
        "text": "What to Expect Before You're Expecting , 2nd edition, Heidi Murkoff. WhatToExpect.com, Ovulation Symptoms: 10 Signs of Ovulation to Know , July 2025. WhatToExpect.com, Fertility Fact Check: What Can Help You Conceive (and What's Just Hype) , January 2026. American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, Fertility Awareness-Based Methods of Family Planning , February 2025. American College of Obstetricians and Gynecologists, Having a Baby After Age 35: How Aging Affects Fertility and Pregnancy , April 2025. American Society for Reproductive Medicine, Fertility in the Aging Female , 2026. March of Dimes, Pregnancy After Age 35 , February 2025. Mayo Clinic, How to Get Pregnant , October 2024. UpToDate, Effects of Advanced Maternal Age on Pregnancy , April 2025.",
        "text_sha256": "4cc8bc698759869262a8697375cd57c2923b2358f5243b6fe36d56b010d14621",
        "word_count": 117
